concepts.content:
The gradient operation is linear with respect to summation. Specifically, for a cost function defined as an average of individual losses:

$$\begin{aligned}
\frac{\partial \frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^N J_i(\theta)}{\partial \theta} = \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^N \frac{\partial J_i(\theta)}{\partial \theta}
\end{aligned}$$

This principle ensures that the gradient of a sum of terms is the sum of the gradients of each term.

